{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And I will send the hornet.</b> Rashi: a species of creature, and it did not cross the Jordan. As for what is written, 'and it shall drive out the Hivite, the Canaanite, etc.' — we say in tractate Sotah: Resh Lakish said, it stood at the bank of the Jordan and injected venom into them. Rav Pappa said, there were two hornets — one in the days of Moses and one in the days of Joshua; that of Moses did not cross, and that of Joshua crossed. And according to the plain sense, it is a metaphor: not by sword and not by bow do I drive them out, but by a light thing."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:08.204837257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}